description: "\"guarantees[5]: Explicit Failure Taxonomy,Root Cause Preservation,Explainable Recovery,Reusable Postmortems,Production Realism\""
spec:
  id: failure_types
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: highest
  module: Ontology
  compiler_stage: Knowledge Representation
  description: "\"\\\"Defines the complete ontology of engineering failures. A failure represents the inability of a software system, process, component or engineering decision to satisfy its intended objectives under given conditions. Every Engineering Knowledge Record involving incidents, debugging, optimization or postmortem analysis shall classify failures using this ontology.\\\"\""
purpose: Represent failures as reusable engineering knowledge rather than isolated bugs.
ekr: "\"\\\"Every failure record contains\\\"[7]: Trigger,Symptoms,Evidence,Root Cause,Mitigation,Recovery,Lessons Learned\""
examples:
  Example_01:
    Failure: Deadlock
    Cause: Circular Wait
    Detection: Thread Dump
    Mitigation: Lock Ordering
  Example_02:
    Failure: Memory Leak
    Cause: Lost References
    Detection: Heap Profile
    Mitigation: Lifetime Analysis
  Example_03:
    Failure: API Timeout
    Cause: Database Lock
    Detection: Distributed Trace
    Mitigation: Query Optimization
  Example_04:
    Failure: Split Brain
    Cause: Network Partition
    Detection: Consensus Metrics
    Mitigation: Quorum Recovery
success: Every engineering failure becomes reusable engineering knowledge.
future:
  failure_prediction: true
  automated_postmortems: true
  causal_failure_graphs: true
  probabilistic_failures: true
  autonomous_recovery: true
